 one variable – the United States center was a gentleman named " [:a {:href "/athletes/7008"} "Bill Russell"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Russell played at the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/4431"} "University of San Francisco"] ", where he led his team to the NCAA title in 1955 and 1956.  A 6-9 center (206 cm.) with very long arms, he emphasized defense and team play and would eventually be considered the greatest champion in the history of American basketball, leading his NBA team, the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/541"} "Boston Celtics"] ", to 10 NBA Championships, eight of them consecutively.  He was assisted by the guard, " [:a {:href "/athletes/6339"} "K. C. Jones"] ", who played throughout his career with Russell, at San Francisco, on the Olympic team, and later with the Boston Celtics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "During the Olympics, the United States’ team was dominant.  They won every game by over 30 points, including the final against the Soviet Union by 89-55."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button160951", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button160951').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Scoring Average"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Disqualifications"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2-point Field Goals Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "2-point Field Goals %"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals Made"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "3-point Field Goals %"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Total Fi